% SOURCE: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridge_and_torch_problem
% (fetched 2026-10-09), problem statement verbatim:
%
% "Four people come to a river in the night."
% "There is a narrow bridge, and it can only hold two people at a
%  time."
% "They have one torch and, because it's night, the torch has to be
%  used when crossing the bridge."
% "Person A can cross the bridge in 1 minute, B in 2 minutes, C in 5
%  minutes, and D in 8 minutes."
% "When two people cross the bridge together, they must move at the
%  slower person's pace."
% "The question is, can they all get across the bridge if the torch
%  lasts only 15 minutes?"
%
% Formalized from the statement alone — no solution consulted. The
% torch IS the resource: a fuse of 15 wick tokens; a crossing burns
% wick equal to its duration (the slower pace). LLP rules consume
% fixed multisets, so the durations 1/2/5/8 become one crossing rule
% per cost class, with bwd facts naming who/which pair burns at that
% rate. The question "can they all get across in 15" = P[solved] > 0.
catalog bridge 1.
provenance text "bridge and torch: four people, two at a time at the slower pace, one torch of 15 minutes" "2026-10-09".
layers (dyn).
stages (walk).
type person {a b c d}.
type side {near far}.
namespace br produce (dyn).
pred pos(person, side) : br.
pred torch(side) : br.
pred wick : br.
pred solved : br.
pred tally : br.
bwd across(side, side).
across(near, far).
across(far, near).
bwd pace1(person).
pace1(a).
bwd pace2(person).
pace2(b).
bwd pace5(person).
pace5(c).
bwd pace8(person).
pace8(d).
bwd max2(person, person).
max2(a, b).
bwd max5(person, person).
max5(a, c).
max5(b, c).
bwd max8(person, person).
max8(a, d).
max8(b, d).
max8(c, d).
stage walk {
  %% "Person A can cross the bridge in 1 minute" — alone, "the torch has to be used when crossing"
  solo1 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pace1(X) * across(S, T) * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T).
  %% "B in 2 minutes"
  solo2 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pace2(X) * across(S, T) * wick * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T).
  %% "C in 5 minutes"
  solo5 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pace5(X) * across(S, T) * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T).
  %% "and D in 8 minutes"
  solo8 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pace8(X) * across(S, T) * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T).
  %% "it can only hold two people at a time" / "they must move at the slower person's pace"
  pair2 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pos(Y, S) * max2(X, Y) * across(S, T) * wick * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T) * pos(Y, T).
  %% "they must move at the slower person's pace"
  pair5 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pos(Y, S) * max5(X, Y) * across(S, T) * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T) * pos(Y, T).
  %% "they must move at the slower person's pace"
  pair8 [dyn] : torch(S) * pos(X, S) * pos(Y, S) * max8(X, Y) * across(S, T) * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick * wick -o torch(T) * pos(X, T) * pos(Y, T).
  %% "can they all get across the bridge"
  done [dyn] : tally * $pos(a, far) * $pos(b, far) * $pos(c, far) * $pos(d, far) -o solved.
}
#init pos(a,near) 1
#init pos(b,near) 1
#init pos(c,near) 1
#init pos(d,near) 1
#init torch(near) 1
#init wick 15
#init tally 1
#steps 20
